we're going to begin with breaking news  that could mean trouble for one of  america's closest middle east allies  the united nations report on the killing  of washington post contributor jamal  khashoggi  recommends an investigation of saudi  arabia's powerful crown prince mohammed  bin salman  his role has been a source of  speculation since khashoggi was murdered  the report says quote there is credible  evidence meriting further investigation  holly williams has covered this case  from the very beginning and she's in  istanbul  where khashoggi was killed at the saudi  consulate back in october  so holly good morning to you but what  does the report say warning this  report will undoubtedly infuriate the  government of saudi arabia  mainly because of that key headline that  quote  there is credible evidence warranting  further investigation  that crown prince mohammed bin salman  was involved in the killing of jamal  khashoggi  the saudis have consistently denied that  even as they've changed their story  more than once about what actually  happened and despite widespread  suspicions that the crown prince is  implicated  just a reminder of the facts here jamal  khashoggi a saudi journalist commentator  and critic of the government  visited the saudi consulate here in  istanbul turkey in october last year  never to be seen again at first the  saudi government denied all involvement  then more than two weeks later they  finally admitted he'd been killed inside  the consulate  they claimed in a physical altercation  then  weeks later they said he'd actually been  killed by a lethal injection in a rogue  operation  jamal shokoji's body has never been  found the un report also found that the  trial in saudi arabia of 11 suspects  fails to meet procedural standards and  should be suspended  it's being held behind closed doors and  the fear is that some of those suspects  could be put to death without the  opportunity to tell their stories to the  outside world  tony holly what does this mean for the  u.s relationship with saudi arabia  i think the key thing tony is that it  increases the pressure on the us  government  uh to take a tougher line with the  saudis uh beyond the sanctions on  individuals uh that are already in place  and specifically with respect to the  crown prince mohammed bin salman  all right holly williams for us in  istanbul holly thank you very much
 

